      "hints": [
        "Set $x = 0$ in the circle equation $(x - 3)^2 + (y - 5)^2 = 40$.",
        "Solve $(0 - 3)^2 + (y - 5)^2 = 40 \\implies 9 + (y - 5)^2 = 40 \\implies (y - 5)^2 = 31$.",
        "Take square roots to express $y$ in surd form."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Substitute $x = 0$ into the circle equation to find the $y$-intercepts:\n$$(0 - 3)^2 + (y - 5)^2 = 40 \\implies 9 + (y - 5)^2 = 40$$",
        "Isolate the squared binomial:\n$$(y - 5)^2 = 31$$",
        "Take square roots to find the $y$-coordinates of $A$ and $B$:\n$$y - 5 = \\pm\\sqrt{31} \\implies y = 5 \\pm \\sqrt{31}$$"
      ],
