        "The diameter $AB$ lies on the $y$-axis between $(0, 5 - \\sqrt{31})$ and $(0, 5 + \\sqrt{31})$.",
        "The centre of this circle is the midpoint $(0, 5)$.",
        "The radius is $\\sqrt{31}$, so the radius squared is $31$.",
        "Write down the standard equation of the circle."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Find the centre of the circle as the midpoint of $A(0, 5 - \\sqrt{31})$ and $B(0, 5 + \\sqrt{31})$:\n$$\\text{Centre} = \\left(0, \\frac{(5 - \\sqrt{31}) + (5 + \\sqrt{31})}{2}\\right) = (0, 5)$$",
        "Determine the radius from the midpoint to either endpoint:\n$$r = \\frac{|(5 + \\sqrt{31}) - (5 - \\sqrt{31})|}{2} = \\frac{2\\sqrt{31}}{2} = \\sqrt{31} \\implies r^2 = 31$$",
        "Write the equation of the circle:\n$$(x - 0)^2 + (y - 5)^2 = 31 \\implies x^2 + (y - 5)^2 = 31$$"
